  "limitations": [
    "Candidate interface is a structural superset,not a certified legal mask or completePvP action space. Default placement/boardtargets only;ChooseOne omitted. Candidate stats/observations do not certify all hidden-information rules or adequate Markov state.",
    "Synchronous policy must be pure;clock/log/RNG guard is not a full mutation fingerprint or security sandbox. An engine rejection may have side effects;host must discard ratherthanretry. New generic counters are not yet integrated into productionNNTrain because its main policy remainsGreedy.",
    "16actionfeatures are a separate schema. Existing valueMLP stays745stateinputs;no trained action network or action-index labels yet.20mixed-unit oracle-directed runs are software regression checks,not client rule authority.",
    "Model binary hash binding is deliberately conservative:comments/build metadata/configuration may change the library hash. Regenerate data/retrain using the same runtime artifact after a binary change. JSON/hash metadata is not a signed authority or semantic rule proof.",
    "RuntimeNnPolicy checkssampling/objective/library butdoesnotverify the actual suppliedCardVecs/runtimeJSON. NNTrain compares declared datasetJSON hashes;low-level Predict can be called without contract checks. Runtime data-source validation remains open.",
    "Rollout-mode sampling family checks do not prove all evaluation states fall inside the training distribution,including terminal/budget-exit/side-effectful probes. Pair models are explicitly rejected as probability models here.",
    "Old unbound models remain readable for inspection but strict consumers reject them. LegacyGate1 data must be regenerated for bound training. No inference of missing metadata.",
    "No engine/IR/native rule or whole-card certification promoted;prior3QueenOwnlong seeds remain historical rejection seeds. One-epoch smoke and deterministic traces do not establish AI strength or total audit completion."
  ],
